+# Ultimate Training Modpack v7.1.1 compatibility
+
+This change supports the original Skyline plugins from the
+[official v7.1.1 release](https://github.com/jugeeya/UltimateTrainingModpack/releases/tag/v7.1.1).
+The ZIP SHA-256 used for local validation was
+`edf1ca8fdf479feb801e6afacc3abf440e05263af9f5d872d0d16978fb6590d9`.
+No game data or compiled plugin/game binaries are included in this change.
+
+## Runtime changes
+
+- `nn::account::GetLastOpenedUser(Uid*)` returns the single local account after
+  it has been opened, or the invalid zero Uid beforehand. It writes 16 bytes
+  and does not itself open a user session.
+- `nn::oe::GetPseudoDeviceId` persists a randomly generated, anonymous 16-byte
+  UUID in the selected user-data directory. It does not read hardware IDs.
+- The plugin resolver aliases `nnsocketGetAddrInfo` and `nnsocketFreeAddrInfo`
+  use the existing guest `addrinfo` ABI and offline resolver error handling.
+- Both lifters now handle integer ORR/BIC immediates, REV16, unsigned widening
+  addition/multiplication/accumulation, vector MLA/MLS and by-element MLA/SQDMULH.
+  Sources are captured before destination writes, including aliased registers.
+- `SSBU_NRO_IMPORT_REPORT=1` prints all unresolved module imports for diagnosis.
+  It does not suppress traps or change import resolution.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+On a local Windows Smash 13.0.5 build, using copied saves and a separate SD
+profile, the unchanged NROs initialize and reach real training gameplay.
+The menu opens and accepts/saves settings; settings reload after a restart;
+the configured CPU Jump/Always action runs; colored hitbox spheres render during
+a Mewtwo aerial; saving, moving and restoring fighter positions works.
+The plugin build reports one untranslated instruction, an intentional UDF,
+and zero untranslated instructions classified as real code.
+
+`tests/simd_immediate_test.py --clang <clang>` compares 868 generated-code cases
+against Unicorn for both lifters, including destination aliasing, saturation
+and upper-half clearing. Requires Unicorn and a Windows C compiler. The SDK
+self-tests also cover account output bounds and persistent UUID output bounds.
+
+This is not a verification of every fighter, stage, training option or mod
+combination. Four lua2cpp imports are initially unresolved and are rebound when
+the common module loads. The weak NRO header symbol and imports on unused
+network/TLS/clock paths remain unresolved; general HTTPS/updater support was
+not added. Offline DNS failures remain real failures, not fabricated successes.
+No hook offsets were added for this mod: the existing discovery and local
+re-lifting mechanism records the sites for the user's own game version.
+
+## Installation
+
+Apply this source change to OpenSmash and the accompanying Mod Manager change.
+Use your own complete 13.0.5 build and the normal local compiler dependencies.
+Import the original `TrainingModpack.zip` in the updated manager, activate
+**Ultimate Training Modpack v7.1.1**, and choose **Mit Mods spielen**.
+The first build records and recompiles the needed hooks and can take minutes.
+Open the training menu with Special + Up Taunt (default keyboard: X + I).
+Vanilla continues to use the original game executable.
